  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: Build a highly cinematic, interactive, visually stunning hackathon event website called **TRANSFORMX**.\n\nThe visual inspiration is the mechanical sci-fi aesthetic of Optimus Prime and transforming robots: metallic armor, mechanical panels, futuristic vehicle components, glowing energy cores, tactical HUD interfaces, industrial machinery, and cinematic transformation sequences.\n\nIMPORTANT: Do NOT create a generic AI-generated website with ordinary rounded cards, gradient blobs, glassmorphism, excessive neon, or a standard startup landing page layout. The website should feel like an interactive cinematic experience and a futuristic command interface.\n\n---\n\n# CORE DESIGN LANGUAGE\n\n## Visual Style\n\nUse a dark cinematic background with:\n\n* Deep metallic navy and black\n* Optimus-inspired red armor accents\n* Electric blue energy lights\n* Silver and gunmetal mechanical surfaces\n* Small glowing cyan HUD elements\n* Occasional orange/yellow warning indicators\n\nThe UI should resemble mechanical armor and a futuristic cybernetic command console.\n\nAvoid simple rectangular cards.\n\nEvery container, panel, button, and section should have mechanical details such as:\n\n* Armor plate edges\n* Angular cuts\n* Mechanical joints\n* Bolts\n* Energy lines\n* Small technical labels\n* HUD brackets\n* Metallic borders\n* Animated scanning lines\n* Glowing energy cores\n* Circuit patterns\n\nThe design must feel premium, cinematic, responsive, and intentionally designed.\n\n---\n\n# WEBSITE INTRO / LOADING EXPERIENCE\n\nCreate a full-screen cinematic introduction.\n\nInitially, the screen should be dark.\n\nA futuristic mechanical sword inspired by Optimus Prime should dramatically swoop into the screen with motion blur and metallic sound effects.\n\nThe sword should:\n\n1. Enter the screen with a cinematic swooping motion.\n2. Rotate slightly.\n3. Strike through the center of the screen.\n4. Create a glowing energy slash.\n5. Divide the screen into two mechanical halves.\n6. The two halves should slide apart like transforming armor panels.\n7. Behind them, reveal the event name:\n\n# TRANSFORMX\n\nThe text should appear as if it is being assembled from mechanical components.\n\nAdd metallic transformation sounds, servo sounds, energy charging effects, and a cinematic impact sound.\n\nBelow the title display a catchy hackathon phrase:\n\n**TRANSFORM. BUILD. DEPLOY THE FUTURE.**\n\nAlternative tagline styling can include animated words where:\n\nTRANSFORM \342\206\222 BUILD \342\206\222 DEPLOY\n\nlight up sequentially.\n\nAfter the intro animation completes, smoothly transition into the main website.\n\nThe intro should be skippable.\n\n---\n\n# CURSOR\n\nCreate a custom cursor inspired by a futuristic targeting system.\n\nThe cursor should include:\n\n* Small mechanical brackets\n* A glowing blue center\n* Rotating targeting rings\n* A subtle trailing energy effect\n\nWhen hovering over buttons or interactive elements:\n\n* The cursor should transform slightly.\n* HUD brackets should expand.\n* A mechanical click sound can play.\n\nKeep the cursor smooth and responsive.\n\n---\n\n# SOUND SYSTEM\n\nCreate an optional sound experience.\n\nAdd a small sound control button in the top navigation.\n\nSound effects should include:\n\n* Mechanical servo movement\n* Metallic armor movement\n* Futuristic UI beeps\n* Energy charging sounds\n* Subtle transformation sounds\n* Button interaction sounds\n\nThe website must NOT automatically play loud music.\n\nSound should begin only after user interaction.\n\nProvide:\n\nSOUND: ON / OFF\n\nwith a futuristic HUD-style toggle.\n\n---\n\n# NAVIGATION\n\nCreate a floating futuristic navigation interface.\n\nSections:\n\nHOME\nEVENT\nTHEMES\nROADMAP\nREGISTER\n\nThe navigation should look like a mechanical HUD component rather than a standard navbar.\n\nOn scroll:\n\n* Sections should highlight.\n* Small scanning effects should move across the navigation.\n* The active section should glow blue/red.\n\n---\n\n# HERO SECTION\n\nAfter the cinematic intro, reveal the hero section.\n\nDisplay:\n\nTRANSFORMX\n\nSubtitle:\n\n**TRANSFORM. BUILD. DEPLOY THE FUTURE.**\n\nAdd a short description:\n\nA high-energy hackathon where ideas transform into intelligent solutions.\n\nThe background should include subtle mechanical movement.\n\nPossible visual elements:\n\n* Rotating mechanical gears\n* Animated circuit patterns\n* Moving energy particles\n* Floating HUD elements\n* Mechanical vehicle silhouettes\n* Animated metallic armor panels\n\nDo not overcrowd the hero section.\n\nMake TRANSFORMX the visual focus.\n\n---\n\n# COUNTDOWN TIMER\n\nCreate a large futuristic countdown timer counting down to:\n\n25 SEPTEMBER 2026\n\nDisplay:\n\nDAYS : HOURS : MINUTES : SECONDS\n\nExample:\n\n023 : 14 : 32 : 08\n\nEach time unit should appear inside a mechanical module inspired by futuristic vehicle and robot components.\n\nThe countdown boxes should NOT be simple rounded cards.\n\nUse:\n\n* Metallic frames\n* Angular cuts\n* Small bolts\n* Energy lights\n* Digital display typography\n* Animated numbers\n\nWhen numbers change, add a subtle mechanical flip or digital transition.\n\n---\n\n# PIXELATED GUIDE CHARACTER\n\nCreate a small pixel-art robotic commander inspired by Optimus Prime aesthetics.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not use an exact copyrighted character model or exact reproduction.\n\nCreate an original pixel-art robotic commander with:\n\n* Blue armor\n* Red armor accents\n* A heroic mechanical silhouette\n* Futuristic glowing eyes\n\nPosition the character near the bottom corner of the screen.\n\nThe character should have a futuristic speech bubble.\n\nWhen the user first opens the website, the character should guide them through the website.\n\nExample dialogue:\n\n\"COMMAND LINK ESTABLISHED.\"\n\n\"Welcome, builder.\"\n\n\"Scroll to explore the mission.\"\n\nWhen the user reaches sections, the character can provide small contextual explanations.\n\nExamples:\n\nEVENT DETAILS:\n\"MISSION PARAMETERS DETECTED.\"\n\nTHEMES:\n\"SEVEN DOMAINS. UNLIMITED POSSIBILITIES.\"\n\nROADMAP:\n\"TRACK YOUR JOURNEY. COMPLETE EACH PHASE.\"\n\nREGISTER:\n\"YOUR NEXT MISSION AWAITS.\"\n\nThe guide should be dismissible and should not obstruct the content.\n\n---\n\n# EVENT DETAILS SECTION\n\nCreate an Event Details section designed like a futuristic command dashboard.\n\nDisplay the following:\n\n## EVENT DATE\n\n25 SEPTEMBER 2026\n\n## DURATION\n\n8 HOURS\n\n## FUEL PROVISION\n\nSNACKS PROVIDED\n\nInstead of ordinary cards, create three mechanical modules inspired by different transforming machine components.\n\nFor example:\n\nDATE \342\206\222 Inspired by a mechanical chest armor module\n\nDURATION \342\206\222 Inspired by an energy core or vehicle dashboard\n\nSNACKS \342\206\222 Inspired by a futuristic supply module\n\nEach module should animate when entering the viewport.\n\nAdd:\n\n* Mechanical opening animation\n* Energy glow\n* HUD scanning effect\n* Small technical labels\n\n---\n\n# REGISTER SECTION\n\nCreate a large, highly noticeable REGISTER button.\n\nThe button should resemble a futuristic transformation control panel.\n\nButton text:\n\nINITIATE REGISTRATION\n\nWhen clicked:\n\nOpen the Google Form link in a new tab.\n\nUse a placeholder variable:\n\nGOOGLE_FORM_URL\n\nI will replace this with the actual Google Form URL later.\n\nHover animation:\n\n* Mechanical parts shift.\n* Energy lines activate.\n* Blue and red lights power up.\n* Text changes to:\n\nPROCEED \342\206\222\n\n---\n\n# SIH THEMES SECTION\n\nCreate a visually spectacular section for the seven SIH Themes.\n\nDo NOT display them as a boring grid of normal cards.\n\nCreate seven interactive mechanical modules arranged in an interesting formation.\n\nPossible concepts:\n\n* A futuristic command bay\n* A rotating mechanical ring\n* A transforming vehicle interface\n* Floating mechanical panels\n* A robotic arm assembly interface\n\nEach theme module should have its own mechanical visual identity inspired by different futuristic machines.\n\nThe seven themes are:\n\n01 \342\200\224 SMART AUTOMATION\n\nIdeas focused on intelligent use of resources and combining Artificial Intelligence with technology to explore various sources and generate valuable insights.\n\n02 \342\200\224 ROBOTICS & DRONES\n\nDesign drones and robots to solve pressing challenges in India, including medical emergencies, search and rescue operations, and other critical applications.\n\n03 \342\200\224 BLOCKCHAIN & CYBERSECURITY\n\nIdeas based on decentralized and distributed ledger technology for securely storing digital information and transforming multiple sectors.\n\n04 \342\200\224 SMART EDUCATION\n\nTechnology-driven education that enables learners to learn more effectively, efficiently, flexibly, and comfortably in the digital age.\n\n05 \342\200\224 SMART VEHICLES\n\nCreating intelligent devices and technologies to improve the transportation and communication sector.\n\n06 \342\200\224 RENEWABLE / SUSTAINABLE ENERGY\n\nInnovative ideas that help generate, manage, and utilize renewable and sustainable energy sources more efficiently.\n\n07 \342\200\224 DISASTER MANAGEMENT\n\nIdeas related to technology-driven solutions for disaster preparedness, early warning, emergency response, rescue operations, and recovery.\n\n---\n\n# THEME INTERACTION\n\nWhen a theme is clicked:\n\nThe selected module should transform.\n\nPossible animation:\n\n* Mechanical panels rotate.\n* Armor pieces separate.\n* Energy lights activate.\n* The selected theme expands into a detailed tactical information panel.\n\nDisplay the following categories:\n\nDOMAIN OVERVIEW\n\nFOCUS AREAS\n\nPOTENTIAL IMPACT\n\nTECHNOLOGY DOMAINS\n\nEach category should contain concise, useful information related to that SIH theme.\n\nThe detail panel should feel like a futuristic mission briefing screen.\n\nUse animated text reveals.\n\nAdd small HUD labels such as:\n\nTARGET DOMAIN\n\nMISSION DATA\n\nTECH STACK\n\nIMPACT VECTOR\n\nOnly one theme should be expanded at a time.\n\n---\n\n# ROADMAP SECTION\n\nCreate an animated vertical or horizontal mission timeline.\n\nDo NOT use a basic timeline.\n\nMake the roadmap feel like a futuristic transformation sequence.\n\nThe roadmap line should resemble:\n\n* A glowing energy transmission line\n* Mechanical rails\n* A futuristic circuit\n* An Energon-style power connection\n\nEach milestone should activate as the user scrolls.\n\nThe milestones are:\n\n---\n\nPHASE_00\n\nREGISTRATION PROTOCOL\n\nParticipant onboarding and team registration sequence initiation.\n\nDATE:\n26 Apr \342\200\223 19 Sep 2026\n\nTIME:\n8:00 AM \342\200\223 11:59 PM\n\n---\n\nROUND_01\n\nNEURAL APTITUDE\n\nTechnical quiz evaluating analytical and problem-solving metrics.\n\nDATE:\n2 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n6:00 PM\n\nSTATUS:\nBROADCAST\n\n---\n\nPHASE I QUALIFICATION\n\nTransmission of shortlisted units from Round 1.\n\nDATE:\n3 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n8:00 PM\n\n---\n\nROUND_02\n\nQUANTUM PROJECT NEXUS\n\nUnits select mission statements and submit structural proposals.\n\nDATE:\n3 May \342\200\223 6 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n6 May 2026, 12:00 PM\n\nSTATUS:\nBROADCAST\n\n---\n\nPHASE II ELITE\n\nTransmission of units shortlisted for the final engagement.\n\nDATE:\n7 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n8:00 PM\n\n---\n\nCRITICAL ENGAGEMENT\n\nQUANTUM ARENA\n\nOffline tactical hackathon. Build and deploy real-time solutions.\n\nDATE:\n8 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n9:00 AM \342\200\223 4:00 PM\n\n---\n\nEach roadmap milestone should have a unique mechanical visual.\n\nPossible inspirations:\n\nPHASE_00:\nA transforming communication module\n\nROUND_01:\nA futuristic scanning system\n\nPHASE I:\nA transmission / signal module\n\nROUND_02:\nA mechanical data core\n\nPHASE II:\nAn elite selection interface\n\nFINAL EVENT:\nA powerful transformation sequence with the largest visual element\n\nAs the user scrolls through the roadmap:\n\n* Energy should travel along the timeline.\n* Each phase should activate.\n* Mechanical parts should unfold.\n* Small sound effects can play if sound is enabled.\n* Completed phases can change color.\n\n---\n\n# ANIMATION SYSTEM\n\nThe entire website should feel alive.\n\nUse smooth animations with performance in mind.\n\nInclude:\n\n* Scroll-triggered animations\n* Parallax movement\n* Mechanical transformations\n* Energy pulses\n* Panel opening animations\n* Rotating components\n* HUD scanning\n* Text reveals\n* Subtle camera-like motion\n\nUse animations purposefully.\n\nDo NOT animate everything constantly.\n\nThe page should alternate between moments of cinematic intensity and clean readable sections.\n\nUse GSAP or another professional animation library where appropriate.\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSIVENESS\n\nThe website must be fully responsive.\n\nDesktop should provide the full cinematic experience.\n\nMobile should maintain the futuristic aesthetic while simplifying complex animations for performance.\n\nThe intro sword animation should work on mobile.\n\nThe countdown should remain readable.\n\nTheme modules should reorganize elegantly.\n\nNavigation should become a futuristic expandable command menu.\n\n---\n\n# PERFORMANCE\n\nOptimize for smooth performance.\n\nUse:\n\n* Lazy loading\n* Optimized 3D assets\n* Compressed textures\n* Reduced animation complexity on mobile\n* Efficient animation loops\n\nRespect prefers-reduced-motion settings.\n\n---\n\n# TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS\n\nBuild using:\n\nReact\n\nThree.js / React Three Fiber for selected 3D elements\n\nGSAP for cinematic and scroll animations\n\nFramer Motion for UI animations where appropriate\n\nCSS/SVG for lightweight mechanical UI elements\n\nCreate reusable components.\n\nSuggested component structure:\n\nIntroSequence\nHero\nCountdown\nRobotGuide\nEventDetails\nThemeSystem\nThemeDetailPanel\nRoadmapTimeline\nRegistration\nNavigation\nSoundController\n\nKeep code modular and production-ready.\n\n---\n\n# FINAL DESIGN GOAL\n\nThe final website should feel like entering a futuristic robotic command center before a major mission.\n\nThe user should not feel like they are simply scrolling through a website.\n\nThey should feel like they are progressing through an interactive cinematic experience.\n\nEvery major section should have its own transformation moment.\n\nThe visual identity should remain consistent throughout:\n\nMETALLIC.\nMECHANICAL.\nHEROIC.\nFUTURISTIC.\nENERGY-POWERED.\n\nThe final experience should be premium, smooth, visually memorable, highly animated, and completely different from a typical hackathon landing page.\n\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: Build a highly cinematic, interactive, visually stunning hackathon event website called **TRANSFORMX**.\n\nThe visual inspiration is the mechanical sci-fi aesthetic of Optimus Prime and transforming robots: metallic armor, mechanical panels, futuristic vehicle components, glowing energy cores, tactical HUD interfaces, industrial machinery, and cinematic transformation sequences.\n\nIMPORTANT: Do NOT create a generic AI-generated website with ordinary rounded cards, gradient blobs, glassmorphism, excessive neon, or a standard startup landing page layout. The website should feel like an interactive cinematic experience and a futuristic command interface.\n\n---\n\n# CORE DESIGN LANGUAGE\n\n## Visual Style\n\nUse a dark cinematic background with:\n\n* Deep metallic navy and black\n* Optimus-inspired red armor accents\n* Electric blue energy lights\n* Silver and gunmetal mechanical surfaces\n* Small glowing cyan HUD elements\n* Occasional orange/yellow warning indicators\n\nThe UI should resemble mechanical armor and a futuristic cybernetic command console.\n\nAvoid simple rectangular cards.\n\nEvery container, panel, button, and section should have mechanical details such as:\n\n* Armor plate edges\n* Angular cuts\n* Mechanical joints\n* Bolts\n* Energy lines\n* Small technical labels\n* HUD brackets\n* Metallic borders\n* Animated scanning lines\n* Glowing energy cores\n* Circuit patterns\n\nThe design must feel premium, cinematic, responsive, and intentionally designed.\n\n---\n\n# WEBSITE INTRO / LOADING EXPERIENCE\n\nCreate a full-screen cinematic introduction.\n\nInitially, the screen should be dark.\n\nA futuristic mechanical sword inspired by Optimus Prime should dramatically swoop into the screen with motion blur and metallic sound effects.\n\nThe sword should:\n\n1. Enter the screen with a cinematic swooping motion.\n2. Rotate slightly.\n3. Strike through the center of the screen.\n4. Create a glowing energy slash.\n5. Divide the screen into two mechanical halves.\n6. The two halves should slide apart like transforming armor panels.\n7. Behind them, reveal the event name:\n\n# TRANSFORMX\n\nThe text should appear as if it is being assembled from mechanical components.\n\nAdd metallic transformation sounds, servo sounds, energy charging effects, and a cinematic impact sound.\n\nBelow the title display a catchy hackathon phrase:\n\n**TRANSFORM. BUILD. DEPLOY THE FUTURE.**\n\nAlternative tagline styling can include animated words where:\n\nTRANSFORM \342\206\222 BUILD \342\206\222 DEPLOY\n\nlight up sequentially.\n\nAfter the intro animation completes, smoothly transition into the main website.\n\nThe intro should be skippable.\n\n---\n\n# CURSOR\n\nCreate a custom cursor inspired by a futuristic targeting system.\n\nThe cursor should include:\n\n* Small mechanical brackets\n* A glowing blue center\n* Rotating targeting rings\n* A subtle trailing energy effect\n\nWhen hovering over buttons or interactive elements:\n\n* The cursor should transform slightly.\n* HUD brackets should expand.\n* A mechanical click sound can play.\n\nKeep the cursor smooth and responsive.\n\n---\n\n# SOUND SYSTEM\n\nCreate an optional sound experience.\n\nAdd a small sound control button in the top navigation.\n\nSound effects should include:\n\n* Mechanical servo movement\n* Metallic armor movement\n* Futuristic UI beeps\n* Energy charging sounds\n* Subtle transformation sounds\n* Button interaction sounds\n\nThe website must NOT automatically play loud music.\n\nSound should begin only after user interaction.\n\nProvide:\n\nSOUND: ON / OFF\n\nwith a futuristic HUD-style toggle.\n\n---\n\n# NAVIGATION\n\nCreate a floating futuristic navigation interface.\n\nSections:\n\nHOME\nEVENT\nTHEMES\nROADMAP\nREGISTER\n\nThe navigation should look like a mechanical HUD component rather than a standard navbar.\n\nOn scroll:\n\n* Sections should highlight.\n* Small scanning effects should move across the navigation.\n* The active section should glow blue/red.\n\n---\n\n# HERO SECTION\n\nAfter the cinematic intro, reveal the hero section.\n\nDisplay:\n\nTRANSFORMX\n\nSubtitle:\n\n**TRANSFORM. BUILD. DEPLOY THE FUTURE.**\n\nAdd a short description:\n\nA high-energy hackathon where ideas transform into intelligent solutions.\n\nThe background should include subtle mechanical movement.\n\nPossible visual elements:\n\n* Rotating mechanical gears\n* Animated circuit patterns\n* Moving energy particles\n* Floating HUD elements\n* Mechanical vehicle silhouettes\n* Animated metallic armor panels\n\nDo not overcrowd the hero section.\n\nMake TRANSFORMX the visual focus.\n\n---\n\n# COUNTDOWN TIMER\n\nCreate a large futuristic countdown timer counting down to:\n\n25 SEPTEMBER 2026\n\nDisplay:\n\nDAYS : HOURS : MINUTES : SECONDS\n\nExample:\n\n023 : 14 : 32 : 08\n\nEach time unit should appear inside a mechanical module inspired by futuristic vehicle and robot components.\n\nThe countdown boxes should NOT be simple rounded cards.\n\nUse:\n\n* Metallic frames\n* Angular cuts\n* Small bolts\n* Energy lights\n* Digital display typography\n* Animated numbers\n\nWhen numbers change, add a subtle mechanical flip or digital transition.\n\n---\n\n# PIXELATED GUIDE CHARACTER\n\nCreate a small pixel-art robotic commander inspired by Optimus Prime aesthetics.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo not use an exact copyrighted character model or exact reproduction.\n\nCreate an original pixel-art robotic commander with:\n\n* Blue armor\n* Red armor accents\n* A heroic mechanical silhouette\n* Futuristic glowing eyes\n\nPosition the character near the bottom corner of the screen.\n\nThe character should have a futuristic speech bubble.\n\nWhen the user first opens the website, the character should guide them through the website.\n\nExample dialogue:\n\n\"COMMAND LINK ESTABLISHED.\"\n\n\"Welcome, builder.\"\n\n\"Scroll to explore the mission.\"\n\nWhen the user reaches sections, the character can provide small contextual explanations.\n\nExamples:\n\nEVENT DETAILS:\n\"MISSION PARAMETERS DETECTED.\"\n\nTHEMES:\n\"SEVEN DOMAINS. UNLIMITED POSSIBILITIES.\"\n\nROADMAP:\n\"TRACK YOUR JOURNEY. COMPLETE EACH PHASE.\"\n\nREGISTER:\n\"YOUR NEXT MISSION AWAITS.\"\n\nThe guide should be dismissible and should not obstruct the content.\n\n---\n\n# EVENT DETAILS SECTION\n\nCreate an Event Details section designed like a futuristic command dashboard.\n\nDisplay the following:\n\n## EVENT DATE\n\n25 SEPTEMBER 2026\n\n## DURATION\n\n8 HOURS\n\n## FUEL PROVISION\n\nSNACKS PROVIDED\n\nInstead of ordinary cards, create three mechanical modules inspired by different transforming machine components.\n\nFor example:\n\nDATE \342\206\222 Inspired by a mechanical chest armor module\n\nDURATION \342\206\222 Inspired by an energy core or vehicle dashboard\n\nSNACKS \342\206\222 Inspired by a futuristic supply module\n\nEach module should animate when entering the viewport.\n\nAdd:\n\n* Mechanical opening animation\n* Energy glow\n* HUD scanning effect\n* Small technical labels\n\n---\n\n# REGISTER SECTION\n\nCreate a large, highly noticeable REGISTER button.\n\nThe button should resemble a futuristic transformation control panel.\n\nButton text:\n\nINITIATE REGISTRATION\n\nWhen clicked:\n\nOpen the Google Form link in a new tab.\n\nUse a placeholder variable:\n\nGOOGLE_FORM_URL\n\nI will replace this with the actual Google Form URL later.\n\nHover animation:\n\n* Mechanical parts shift.\n* Energy lines activate.\n* Blue and red lights power up.\n* Text changes to:\n\nPROCEED \342\206\222\n\n---\n\n# SIH THEMES SECTION\n\nCreate a visually spectacular section for the seven SIH Themes.\n\nDo NOT display them as a boring grid of normal cards.\n\nCreate seven interactive mechanical modules arranged in an interesting formation.\n\nPossible concepts:\n\n* A futuristic command bay\n* A rotating mechanical ring\n* A transforming vehicle interface\n* Floating mechanical panels\n* A robotic arm assembly interface\n\nEach theme module should have its own mechanical visual identity inspired by different futuristic machines.\n\nThe seven themes are:\n\n01 \342\200\224 SMART AUTOMATION\n\nIdeas focused on intelligent use of resources and combining Artificial Intelligence with technology to explore various sources and generate valuable insights.\n\n02 \342\200\224 ROBOTICS & DRONES\n\nDesign drones and robots to solve pressing challenges in India, including medical emergencies, search and rescue operations, and other critical applications.\n\n03 \342\200\224 BLOCKCHAIN & CYBERSECURITY\n\nIdeas based on decentralized and distributed ledger technology for securely storing digital information and transforming multiple sectors.\n\n04 \342\200\224 SMART EDUCATION\n\nTechnology-driven education that enables learners to learn more effectively, efficiently, flexibly, and comfortably in the digital age.\n\n05 \342\200\224 SMART VEHICLES\n\nCreating intelligent devices and technologies to improve the transportation and communication sector.\n\n06 \342\200\224 RENEWABLE / SUSTAINABLE ENERGY\n\nInnovative ideas that help generate, manage, and utilize renewable and sustainable energy sources more efficiently.\n\n07 \342\200\224 DISASTER MANAGEMENT\n\nIdeas related to technology-driven solutions for disaster preparedness, early warning, emergency response, rescue operations, and recovery.\n\n---\n\n# THEME INTERACTION\n\nWhen a theme is clicked:\n\nThe selected module should transform.\n\nPossible animation:\n\n* Mechanical panels rotate.\n* Armor pieces separate.\n* Energy lights activate.\n* The selected theme expands into a detailed tactical information panel.\n\nDisplay the following categories:\n\nDOMAIN OVERVIEW\n\nFOCUS AREAS\n\nPOTENTIAL IMPACT\n\nTECHNOLOGY DOMAINS\n\nEach category should contain concise, useful information related to that SIH theme.\n\nThe detail panel should feel like a futuristic mission briefing screen.\n\nUse animated text reveals.\n\nAdd small HUD labels such as:\n\nTARGET DOMAIN\n\nMISSION DATA\n\nTECH STACK\n\nIMPACT VECTOR\n\nOnly one theme should be expanded at a time.\n\n---\n\n# ROADMAP SECTION\n\nCreate an animated vertical or horizontal mission timeline.\n\nDo NOT use a basic timeline.\n\nMake the roadmap feel like a futuristic transformation sequence.\n\nThe roadmap line should resemble:\n\n* A glowing energy transmission line\n* Mechanical rails\n* A futuristic circuit\n* An Energon-style power connection\n\nEach milestone should activate as the user scrolls.\n\nThe milestones are:\n\n---\n\nPHASE_00\n\nREGISTRATION PROTOCOL\n\nParticipant onboarding and team registration sequence initiation.\n\nDATE:\n26 Apr \342\200\223 19 Sep 2026\n\nTIME:\n8:00 AM \342\200\223 11:59 PM\n\n---\n\nROUND_01\n\nNEURAL APTITUDE\n\nTechnical quiz evaluating analytical and problem-solving metrics.\n\nDATE:\n2 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n6:00 PM\n\nSTATUS:\nBROADCAST\n\n---\n\nPHASE I QUALIFICATION\n\nTransmission of shortlisted units from Round 1.\n\nDATE:\n3 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n8:00 PM\n\n---\n\nROUND_02\n\nQUANTUM PROJECT NEXUS\n\nUnits select mission statements and submit structural proposals.\n\nDATE:\n3 May \342\200\223 6 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n6 May 2026, 12:00 PM\n\nSTATUS:\nBROADCAST\n\n---\n\nPHASE II ELITE\n\nTransmission of units shortlisted for the final engagement.\n\nDATE:\n7 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n8:00 PM\n\n---\n\nCRITICAL ENGAGEMENT\n\nQUANTUM ARENA\n\nOffline tactical hackathon. Build and deploy real-time solutions.\n\nDATE:\n8 May 2026\n\nTIME:\n9:00 AM \342\200\223 4:00 PM\n\n---\n\nEach roadmap milestone should have a unique mechanical visual.\n\nPossible inspirations:\n\nPHASE_00:\nA transforming communication module\n\nROUND_01:\nA futuristic scanning system\n\nPHASE I:\nA transmission / signal module\n\nROUND_02:\nA mechanical data core\n\nPHASE II:\nAn elite selection interface\n\nFINAL EVENT:\nA powerful transformation sequence with the largest visual element\n\nAs the user scrolls through the roadmap:\n\n* Energy should travel along the timeline.\n* Each phase should activate.\n* Mechanical parts should unfold.\n* Small sound effects can play if sound is enabled.\n* Completed phases can change color.\n\n---\n\n# ANIMATION SYSTEM\n\nThe entire website should feel alive.\n\nUse smooth animations with performance in mind.\n\nInclude:\n\n* Scroll-triggered animations\n* Parallax movement\n* Mechanical transformations\n* Energy pulses\n* Panel opening animations\n* Rotating components\n* HUD scanning\n* Text reveals\n* Subtle camera-like motion\n\nUse animations purposefully.\n\nDo NOT animate everything constantly.\n\nThe page should alternate between moments of cinematic intensity and clean readable sections.\n\nUse GSAP or another professional animation library where appropriate.\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSIVENESS\n\nThe website must be fully responsive.\n\nDesktop should provide the full cinematic experience.\n\nMobile should maintain the futuristic aesthetic while simplifying complex animations for performance.\n\nThe intro sword animation should work on mobile.\n\nThe countdown should remain readable.\n\nTheme modules should reorganize elegantly.\n\nNavigation should become a futuristic expandable command menu.\n\n---\n\n# PERFORMANCE\n\nOptimize for smooth performance.\n\nUse:\n\n* Lazy loading\n* Optimized 3D assets\n* Compressed textures\n* Reduced animation complexity on mobile\n* Efficient animation loops\n\nRespect prefers-reduced-motion settings.\n\n---\n\n# TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS\n\nBuild using:\n\nReact\n\nThree.js / React Three Fiber for selected 3D elements\n\nGSAP for cinematic and scroll animations\n\nFramer Motion for UI animations where appropriate\n\nCSS/SVG for lightweight mechanical UI elements\n\nCreate reusable components.\n\nSuggested component structure:\n\nIntroSequence\nHero\nCountdown\nRobotGuide\nEventDetails\nThemeSystem\nThemeDetailPanel\nRoadmapTimeline\nRegistration\nNavigation\nSoundController\n\nKeep code modular and production-ready.\n\n---\n\n# FINAL DESIGN GOAL\n\nThe final website should feel like entering a futuristic robotic command center before a major mission.\n\nThe user should not feel like they are simply scrolling through a website.\n\nThey should feel like they are progressing through an interactive cinematic experience.\n\nEvery major section should have its own transformation moment.\n\nThe visual identity should remain consistent throughout:\n\nMETALLIC.\nMECHANICAL.\nHEROIC.\nFUTURISTIC.\nENERGY-POWERED.\n\nThe final experience should be premium, smooth, visually memorable, highly animated, and completely different from a typical hackathon landing page.\n\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
  }
