  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Requirements for TRANSFORMX**\n\nI\'m starting to delve into the requirements for **TRANSFORMX**. My initial focus is on the \"Skill Check\" element. I need to ensure a robust system for evaluating available skills, which is the starting point in the development. Further details will be explored to determine the depth of the skill assessment.\n\n\n**Defining Core Visuals**\n\nMy focus has shifted to the core design elements. I\'ve defined a dark, cinematic aesthetic using specific color palettes and metallic textures. The name is set to \"TRANSFORMX - Hackathon Command Portal,\" and the description is \"Cinematic hackathon portal inspired by mechanical sci-fi and transforming robotic command interfaces.\" I\'m updating the metadata and title tags in `index.html` and integrating futuristic Google fonts for a cybernetic look. I want to convey an immersive mechanical sci-fi atmosphere.\n\n\n**Designing UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m concentrating on the UI. I\'ve chosen HUD colors (`#06b6d4`, `#22d3ee`) and warning indicators (`#f59e0b`, `#eab308`). I\'m visualizing mechanical UI with chamfered corners, armor edges, bolt rivets, glowing conduits, and technical decals. The goal is procedural Web Audio for sound, creating synth servo whirs, impacts, and UI clicks, avoiding external files. I have conceptualized a full-screen cinematic intro: Optimus-inspired blade, energy slash, and a mechanical transformation revealing TRANSFORMX.\n\n\n**Crafting Hero Section**\n\nMy attention is now on the hero section\'s aesthetics and functionality. I\'m focusing on \"TRANSFORM. BUILD. DEPLOY THE FUTURE.\" and planning to have the text light up sequentially. The design includes a mechanical HUD with brackets and an energy core glow for the bold typography. I\'m also planning an interactive background featuring rotating gears, a particle energy grid, and transforming armor panels that respond to mouse position. A futuristic cursor is also in development.\n\n\n**Developing Event Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the event countdown timer and guide character. I\'m aiming for a mechanical countdown with metallic module boxes and animated digits. The robotic commander, in pixel art, will guide users with contextual dialogue, including initial greetings and event section prompts.\n\n\n**Elaborating Event Details**\n\nI\'m developing the event details section, conceptualizing three mechanical modules: date (mechanical chest armor), duration (overclocked core), and fuel (tactical crate). These will have interactive inspection modes, sounds, and HUD scanning. I\'m also planning a dismissible registration module with a mechanical sound effect.\n\n\n\n**Constructing Detailed Missions**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed theme information. I\'ve conceptualized a tactical mission briefing panel for each theme, showing an animated unfolding armor plate with labels such as `DOMAIN OVERVIEW` and `TECHNOLOGY DOMAINS`. There will also be a roadmap section with an animated Energon transmission conduit timeline and milestones: registration, aptitude rounds, and qualification phases, and engagement details.\n\n\n"
