  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the development of the **TRANSFORMX** hackathon event website, engineered with a mechanical sci-fi and transforming robotic command aesthetic.\n\n### Key Architectural & Design Implementations\n\n- **Cinematic Introduction Sequence**: \n  - Features an Energon-inspired mechanical sword swooping into view with motion blur, energetic trails, and camera shake.\n  - Strikes through the center to generate a plasma slash that fractures the screen into two heavy blast-shield armor halves that slide apart on hydraulic tracks.\n  - Mechanically assembles the titular **TRANSFORMX** wordmark accompanied by sequential light-up taglines (**TRANSFORM \342\206\222 BUILD \342\206\222 DEPLOY THE FUTURE**), with a quick skip option (`[ESC]`) and replay triggers.\n\n- **Futuristic Targeting Cursor**:\n  - Custom targeting reticle with expanding mechanical corner brackets, rotating reticle rings, precision center core, and real-time cursor coordinate telemetry that locks onto interactive modules with tactical audio feedback.\n\n- **Web Audio Procedural Sound Engine**:\n  - Lightweight, zero-dependency browser Web Audio synthesizer producing servo whirs, armor plate clangs, energy blade slashes, UI capacitor charges, and robotic chatter.\n  - Equipped with a persistent HUD audio controller (`SOUND: ON / OFF`) in the navigation bar.\n\n- **Floating Mechanical Navigation**:\n  - Armored command bar with active section scanning lasers, glowing blue/red status states, quick section jumping, and responsive mobile HUD drawer.\n\n- **Hero & Countdown Module (25 September 2026)**:\n  - Deep metallic navy and gunmetal chassis with layered titanium gears, circuit traces, and high-contrast typography.\n  - Modular vehicle-inspired countdown blocks displaying formatted `DAYS : HOURS : MINUTES : SECONDS` with mechanical corner bolts, status lights, and animated transitions.\n\n- **Pixel-Art Robotic Commander Guide**:\n  - Custom pixel-rendered robotic commander featuring blue and red armor plates, glowing optic visor, and matrix core.\n  - Provides section-aware tactical intel via an interactive cybernetic speech bubble with typewriter text effects and dismissible controls.\n\n- **Event Specifications Dashboard**:\n  - Three distinct transforming machine modules:\n    1. **Event Date (25 Sep 2026)** \342\200\224 Inspired by a mechanical chest armor core.\n    2. **Duration (8 Hours)** \342\200\224 Overclocked plasma tachometer dashboard with rotating energy gauge.\n    3. **Fuel Provision (Snacks Provided)** \342\200\224 Pressurized Energon logistics capsule.\n\n- **Seven SIH Innovation Themes & Mission Briefing Panel**:\n  - Armored command bay formation covering all 7 national innovation domains: *Smart Automation, Robotics & Drones, Blockchain & Cybersecurity, Smart Education, Smart Vehicles, Renewable Energy, and Disaster Management*.\n  - Clicking any theme transforms the module into a **Tactical Mission Briefing Screen** highlighting Domain Overview, Focus Areas, Potential Impact, and Tech Stack domains.\n\n- **Operational Roadmap**:\n  - Glowing Energon transmission conduit tracking all 6 phases (*Registration Protocol, Neural Aptitude, Phase I Qualification, Quantum Project Nexus, Phase II Elite, and Quantum Arena*).\n\n- **Transformation Registration Console**:\n  - Large-scale control panel with hydraulic clamp indicators and a transforming `INITIATE REGISTRATION` button that shifts armor plates and powers up energy conduits on hover to display `PROCEED \342\206\222`, directing to the designated Google Form URL."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Requirements Fulfillment**\n\nI\'ve just finished reviewing the user\'s requirements for the TRANSFORMX website. I\'m pleased to report that the \"Cinematic, interactive, visually stunning\" aspect is addressed. I\'m currently assessing the \"mechanical sci-fi\" aesthetic elements, ensuring they\'re incorporated cohesively. The goal is to ensure all bases are covered.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Style Refinement**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on solidifying the aesthetic direction for TRANSFORMX\'s website. The Optimus Prime inspiration is fully baked in, from the deep metallic navy and electric blue accents to the metallic transformation sound effects. I\'ve also incorporated the user\'s suggestions for the website\'s intro and loading experience, along with the custom cursor and sound system. Navigation is being addressed next.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the development of the **TRANSFORMX** hackathon event website, engineered with a mechanical sci-fi and transforming robotic command aesthetic.\n\n### Key Architectural & Design Implementations\n\n- **Cinematic Introduction Sequence**: \n  - Features an Energon-inspired mechanical sword swooping into view with motion blur, energetic trails, and camera shake.\n  - Strikes through the center to generate a plasma slash that fractures the screen into two heavy blast-shield armor halves that slide apart on hydraulic tracks.\n  - Mechanically assembles the titular **TRANSFORMX** wordmark accompanied by sequential light-up taglines (**TRANSFORM \342\206\222 BUILD \342\206\222 DEPLOY THE FUTURE**), with a quick skip option (`[ESC]`) and replay triggers.\n\n- **Futuristic Targeting Cursor**:\n  - Custom targeting reticle with expanding mechanical corner brackets, rotating reticle rings, precision center core, and real-time cursor coordinate telemetry that locks onto interactive modules with tactical audio feedback.\n\n- **Web Audio Procedural Sound Engine**:\n  - Lightweight, zero-dependency browser Web Audio synthesizer producing servo whirs, armor plate clangs, energy blade slashes, UI capacitor charges, and robotic chatter.\n  - Equipped with a persistent HUD audio controller (`SOUND: ON / OFF`) in the navigation bar.\n\n- **Floating Mechanical Navigation**:\n  - Armored command bar with active section scanning lasers, glowing blue/red status states, quick section jumping, and responsive mobile HUD drawer.\n\n- **Hero & Countdown Module (25 September 2026)**:\n  - Deep metallic navy and gunmetal chassis with layered titanium gears, circuit traces, and high-contrast typography.\n  - Modular vehicle-inspired countdown blocks displaying formatted `DAYS : HOURS : MINUTES : SECONDS` with mechanical corner bolts, status lights, and animated transitions.\n\n- **Pixel-Art Robotic Commander Guide**:\n  - Custom pixel-rendered robotic commander featuring blue and red armor plates, glowing optic visor, and matrix core.\n  - Provides section-aware tactical intel via an interactive cybernetic speech bubble with typewriter text effects and dismissible controls.\n\n- **Event Specifications Dashboard**:\n  - Three distinct transforming machine modules:\n    1. **Event Date (25 Sep 2026)** \342\200\224 Inspired by a mechanical chest armor core.\n    2. **Duration (8 Hours)** \342\200\224 Overclocked plasma tachometer dashboard with rotating energy gauge.\n    3. **Fuel Provision (Snacks Provided)** \342\200\224 Pressurized Energon logistics capsule.\n\n- **Seven SIH Innovation Themes & Mission Briefing Panel**:\n  - Armored command bay formation covering all 7 national innovation domains: *Smart Automation, Robotics & Drones, Blockchain & Cybersecurity, Smart Education, Smart Vehicles, Renewable Energy, and Disaster Management*.\n  - Clicking any theme transforms the module into a **Tactical Mission Briefing Screen** highlighting Domain Overview, Focus Areas, Potential Impact, and Tech Stack domains.\n\n- **Operational Roadmap**:\n  - Glowing Energon transmission conduit tracking all 6 phases (*Registration Protocol, Neural Aptitude, Phase I Qualification, Quantum Project Nexus, Phase II Elite, and Quantum Arena*).\n\n- **Transformation Registration Console**:\n  - Large-scale control panel with hydraulic clamp indicators and a transforming `INITIATE REGISTRATION` button that shifts armor plates and powers up energy conduits on hover to display `PROCEED \342\206\222`, directing to the designated Google Form URL."
